{"qid":"Q41304","names":["Weimar Republic"],"title":"Weimar Republic","endonym":{"native":"Deutsches Reich","lang":"de"},"capsule":"The Weimar Republic (official name Deutsches Reich) was Germany's first sustained parliamentary democracy, proclaimed on 9 November 1918 following the abdication of Kaiser Wilhelm II and governed under the constitution adopted at Weimar on 11 August 1919. Its fourteen years were marked by hyperinflation peaking in November 1923—when a loaf of bread cost 80 billion Reichsmarks—followed by a brief period of relative stability under Gustav Stresemann (foreign minister 1923–1929), then catastrophic depression and political polarisation after 1929. Adolf Hitler's appointment as chancellor on 30 January 1933 and the Enabling Act of 23 March 1933 effectively ended republican government; the attested end date of 1936 corresponds to the period by which all republican institutions had been abolished and Nazi totalitarian structures fully consolidated.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territorial extent is precisely documented; Germany's post-Versailles borders are among the best-surveyed in twentieth-century European history.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Weimar Republic","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Weimar-Republic"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Weimar Republic","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weimar_Republic"}],"britannica":"topic/Weimar-Republic","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Weimar Republic","rulers":[{"qid":"Q57159","name":"Gustav Bauer","start":1919,"end":1920,"image":"Bundesarchiv Bild 183-J0113-0500-001, Gustav Bauer.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bundesarchiv%20Bild%20183-J0113-0500-001%2C%20Gustav%20Bauer.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 de","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q2646","name":"Friedrich Ebert","start":1919,"end":1925,"image":"Friedrich Ebert LCCN2014711530 Trim.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Friedrich%20Ebert%20LCCN2014711530%20Trim.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Hermann Noack","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q77156","name":"Constantin Fehrenbach","start":1920,"end":1921,"image":"Bundesarchiv Bild 183-R18733, Constantin Fehrenbach.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bundesarchiv%20Bild%20183-R18733%2C%20Constantin%20Fehrenbach.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 de","artist":"UnknownUnknown","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q57158","name":"Hermann Müller","start":1920,"end":1920,"image":"Bundesarchiv Bild 146-1979-122-28A, Hermann Müller(cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bundesarchiv%20Bild%20146-1979-122-28A%2C%20Hermann%20M%C3%BCller(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 de","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q60150","name":"Joseph Wirth","start":1921,"end":1922,"image":"Bundesarchiv Bild 146III-105, Joseph Wirth.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bundesarchiv%20Bild%20146III-105%2C%20Joseph%20Wirth.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 de","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q77179","name":"Wilhelm Cuno","start":1922,"end":1923,"image":"Bundesarchiv Bild 183-2002-0625-505, Dr. Wilhelm Cuno (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bundesarchiv%20Bild%20183-2002-0625-505%2C%20Dr.%20Wilhelm%20Cuno%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","i